  "_allowlistMasqueradeNote": "WINDOWS SYSTEM PROCESS NAMES - these are MASQUERADE TRIPWIRES, not conveniences. Natively advertises 'Process Disguise: the app and every one of its helper processes run under a system process name, so a process list shows a system service, not an interview tool.' Each entry below pins the name to BOTH a Microsoft signature AND a \\Windows\\ path, so a real system process is suppressed while anything merely WEARING the name - unsigned, wrongly signed, or running from %LOCALAPPDATA% - is escalated x1.75 with a distinct masquerade finding. A name-only entry here would be a free hiding place; never add one.",

  "_allowlistNote": "Keyed on the TRIPLE (processName, expectedSigner, expectedPathFragment). Full match suppresses to 0.0; name matches but signer/path does not -> MASQUERADE, escalated to 1.75 with a distinct finding; verified=false entries only down-rank to 0.35 and are never hard-suppressed. verified=false means we did not confirm first-hand that this process legitimately trips the hidden-window signal, only that the process name is real.",

